# CLAUDE workspace

This folder is a parent for several independent projects. Open each project directly in your editor rather than working from this directory. Each subproject has its own CLAUDE.md, its own memory directory, and its own conventions.

## Subprojects

_(/newproject adds a line here for each project, in the form `- [name/](name/) — one-line description`.)_

## House rules

- Universal memory (who I am, how I like Claude to work) lives in this folder's memory hub and is symlinked into every subproject by `$WORKSPACE_DIR/scripts/fanout-memory.sh`. Only `feedback_*.md` and `user_*.md` files fan out; `project_*.md` and `reference_*.md` stay local.
- When you save a universal memory, write it to the hub, add its one-line pointer to the hub's MEMORY.md, then run `$WORKSPACE_DIR/scripts/fanout-memory.sh --all` and tell me it now applies everywhere.
- Every subproject is its own git repo. End every working session with /putdown (it commits and pushes). Start the next one with /pickup.
- Never commit .env or any secret file. Check `git status` before committing; never force-add.
- Keep every CLAUDE.md under 250 lines. Anything longer than about 15 lines goes in a docs/ file with a one-line pointer here that says what the file contains.
